  "description": "A sparse lullaby leaves a high G suspended across three bars while the lower chord changes only its bass, E-flat\u2013E\u2013F. The held note becomes the third of E-flat, the minor third of E half-diminished and the ninth above F. Shorter descending phrases lead back to E-flat with a luminous major ninth.",
